# Generic uses of the address pattern of scripts/check-neutral.sh. A row is
#   PATH-ERE <TAB> TEXT-ERE <TAB> why
# PATH-ERE selects the files; the text that TEXT-ERE matches is removed from the line and the rest of the line is scanned again, so a line that holds an allowed use
# and a forbidden one still fails. The rows for words of the private vocabulary are in its [allow] section (NEUTRAL_VOCAB_FILE, NEUTRAL_VOCAB).

^(docs/|test/|CHANGELOG\.md$)	\b(10\.0\.0\.[0-9]{1,3}|10\.0\.249\.1|10\.9\.9\.9|192\.168\.(0\.0|1\.[0-9]{1,3}))\b	addresses and networks that are the data of the inet and cidr tests
